& [Implementation]
  + AttentionTransportEnvelope binds phase kind optional index actual request domain-separated SHA-256 request digest optional reentry frame frame digest retained-prefix echo and explicit claim limits
  + full-prefix iteration compact-reentry iteration and compact terminal reflection are three disjoint validated shapes
  + local validation recomputes request and frame digests and checks all internal shape relationships without canonical history
  + canonical validators recompile the uniquely expected envelope from one Slice6C transport and require total equality
  + ScriptedTransportEnvelopeSet wraps the unchanged validated Slice6C projection and maps every iteration plus terminal reflection to an ordered envelope
  + strict normalized JSON serialization validates the complete set before emission

& [IdentityBoundary]
  + local integrity proves only that carried bytes and carried hashes remain internally coherent
  + canonical binding requires comparison with the validated host-custodied projection
  + retained-prefix commitment identifies omitted history but cannot reconstruct it
  + SHA-256 content commitment is not a keyed signature producer authentication semantic truth or provider admission

& [Adversarial]
  + request frame digest retained-prefix phase index flag nonclaim claim and unknown-field mutations fail local validation
  + a modified request with a freshly coherent digest passes local validation and still fails canonical reconstruction
  + reordered envelopes altered source projection and terminal-versus-iteration shape changes fail the set validator

& [Rollback]
  + transport_envelope module exports tests and documentation are additive and isolated
  + P0 through Slice6C requests transports replay forms and proof remain unchanged

& [Deferred]
  + keyed signatures trust stores producer authentication provider execution compatibility semantic equivalence persistence remote hidden-state effect FPGA and Minecraft remain unimplemented and unactivated
